adb on the USB gadget driver

The component 'usb_adb' is an adb function of the driver 'exynos_usb_gadget' of
'repos/pixel'. It is a client of a Usb_gadget session with the label "adb", so the
driver's config needs a 'function' with this label. The PC's unmodified adb talks to
it, the engine of the protocol is in 'src/lib/adb_engine'.

:'adb logcat': reads the Terminal session "logcat", usually of 'log_ring'. With '-d' it
  ends after the history.
:'adb push', 'adb pull': see the <vfs> node of the config.
:'adb shell': starts a child per stream, from the <shell> node of the config, which
  is the template of the shells. Without this node a shell is refused.

Config, with an example of the values:

! config | name: panther | model: Pixel 7 | device: panther
!   + vfs | + fs

The attributes are what 'adb devices -l' shows. The serial number comes from the
config of the driver.

The PC's adb 35 needs its native USB back end, the libusb one does not report this
device:

! adb kill-server
! export ADB_LIBUSB=0
! adb logcat

The protocol has host tests:

! make -C repos/muesli/src/lib/adb_engine/test

The scenario 'run/usb_adb_pixel' tests the component on the phone with the tool
'tool/usb_adb_check' on the PC.
